{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 73,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Psalm of Asaph. Surely God is good to Israel, to those who are pure in heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But as for me, my feet had almost stumbled; my steps had nearly slipped.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I envied the arrogant when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have no struggle in their death; their bodies are well-fed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are free of the burdens others carry; they are not afflicted like other men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore pride is their necklace; a garment of violence covers them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From their prosperity proceeds iniquity; the imaginations of their hearts run wild.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They mock and speak with malice; with arrogance they threaten oppression.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They set their mouths against the heavens, and their tongues strut across the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So their people return to this place and drink up waters in abundance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked say, “How can God know? Does the Most High have knowledge?”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, these are the wicked — always carefree as they increase their wealth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely in vain I have kept my heart pure; in innocence I have washed my hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am afflicted all day long and punished every morning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I had said, “I will speak this way,” then I would have betrayed Your children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I tried to understand all this, it was troublesome in my sight",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "until I entered God’s sanctuary; then I discerned their end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely You set them on slick ground; You cast them down into ruin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How suddenly they are laid waste, completely swept away by terrors!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like one waking from a dream, so You, O Lord, awaken and despise their form.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When my heart was grieved and I was pierced within,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was senseless and ignorant; I was a brute beast before You.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet I am always with You; You hold my right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You guide me with Your counsel, and later receive me in glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom have I in heaven but You? And on earth I desire no one besides You.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My flesh and my heart may fail, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Those far from You will surely perish; You destroy all who are unfaithful to You.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.73.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.73.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But as for me, it is good to draw near to God. I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may proclaim all Your works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
